Content: Using large logical records (LLRs)     There are two types of logical records (LRECs) in the  z/TPFDF product :    normal LRECs that fit in a single 4-K file block (including any header and trailer information) 
 large logical records (LLRs) that require more than one 4-K file block. 
     All  z/TPFDF  functions and macros work with LRECs that are 4-K or less. However, to access, add, or updates data in LLRs, you must use functions and macros that support buffered access mode (BAM). Many other functions and macros also support LLRs in a limited manner. See  Files and subfiles ,  C language functions , and  General services  for more information about BAM and the other functions and macros that support LLRs. 
 See   z/TPFDF Database Administration  for more information about the structure and format of LLRs.
