Content: Using compiler options to build 64-bit applications   
 To compile code for 64-bit applications, you must use the  LP (64) compiler option. You must be aware that under  LP (64), some compiler options or sub-options are not supported, and that some options or sub-options are ignored during compilation. 
 Note the following compiler options when you compile code under  LP (64): 

 BACKREG   This option is ignored. 
 CHECK   The  STORAGE  suboption is not supported under  LP (64). This means that you cannot use the following built-in functions:   ALLOCSIZE 
 CHECKSTG 
 UNALLOCATED 

 CMPAT   This option is ignored; effectively,  CMPAT(V3)  is always on under  LP (64). 
 COMMON   This option is ignored. 
 DEFAULT   The following sub-options are ignored under  LP (64):   LINKAGE 

 RENT   This option is ignored; effectively,  RENT  is always on under  LP (64). 
 STDSYS   This option is ignored; effectively,  STDSYS  is always on under  LP (64). 
 WRITABLE   This option is ignored.
