[Rank 4] Title: IBM Enterprise PL/I for z/OS Enhancements from V6R1
URL: 
Score: 0.0605497807264328
Content: Enhancements from V6R1     

Performance improvements      The compiler generates better code for some common usage of FIXED DECIMAL and PICTURE variables. 
 The compiler utilizes some of the new hardware instructions. 
 The compiler internally re-formats some user SELECT statements and thereby improving both compile-time and run-time performance. 
 The compiler generates better code for the ORDINALNAME, ORDINALPRED, and ORDINALSUCC built-in functions. 
 The compiler generates better code for the INLIST and INARRAY built-in functions. 


Usability enhancements        The compiler allows extending 31-bit (AMODE 31) PL/I programs to work with 64-bit (AMODE 64) PL/I programs by providing the addressing space needed to handle your growing PL/I program data without requiring you to convert the entire application to 64-bit. With this new feature, 31-bit code can invoke and be invoked by 64-bit code. See  Mixing AMODE 31 and AMODE 64 code . 
 The compiler flags more possible STRINGSIZE conditions. 
 The compiler flags EXEC HANDLE CONDITION and EXEC SQL WHENEVER as violations of RULES(NOGOTO). 
 The compiler flags passing INONLY to INOUT, INONLY to OUTONLY, and NONASGN to ASGN. 
 The compiler supports +DD: in options strings in IBMZIOP. 
 The compiler does not flag risky INONLY parms if OPTIONS(ASSEMBLER). 
 The compiler issues new compiler messages for REPATTERN to avoid runtime errors. 
 The compiler additionally flags at compile-time both risky and poor-performing code.
Enhancements from V6R1
Compiler option enhancements    
 New compiler options:   The  HGPR  compiler option specifies whether the compiler should preserve and restore the high halves of the 64-bit GPRs. 
 The  MAXRUNONIF  compiler option flags code that should probably be rewritten using the INLIST built-in function. 
 The  MAXSTATIC  compiler option causes the compiler to flag STATIC variables that exceed a specified size. 

 Modified compiler options:   The  ARCH  compiler option supports ARCH(14) to generate code that uses instructions available on the 3931-xxx (IBM z16) models in z/Architecture mode.  
 The default of the  BIFPREC  compiler option is now BIFPREC(31). 
 The CHECKFLOAT suboption of the  DECIMAL  compiler option requires the compiler to generate code that will raise the SIZE condition if the source in a FLOAT to FIXED DECIMAL conversions is too big.  
 The FOFLONADD and NOFOFLONADD suboptions of the  DECIMAL  compiler option require the compiler to generate code that will raise the FIXEDOVERFLOW condition or produce a truncated result for any use of the ADD or SUBTRACT built-in function.  
 The KEEPMINUS suboption of the  DECIMAL  compiler option requires the compiler, under certain circumstances, to generate code that will preserve a "negative zero" in FIXED DECIMAL assignments.  
 The HASH suboption of the  FILEREF  compiler option specifies that each line in the file reference table is followed by a line containing the hex value of a 256-bit SHA-2 hash of that file. 
 The  HEADER  compiler option introduces an additional pair of suboptions: ALL and FIRST. The ALL suboption is the default setting. 
 The  INCPDS  compiler option now supports multiple specifications, allowing you to specify more than one PDS(E) in which INCLUDE files can be found. 
 The ENCODING suboption of the  JSON  compiler option specifies the code page of the JSON text in JSONPUT and JSONGET functions.
