[Rank 5] Title: IBM Enterprise PL/I for z/OS Enhancements in this release
URL: 
Score: 0.034043777734041214
Content: Enhancements in this release   
 This release provides the following functional enhancements that are described in this and the other IBM®  PL/I  books. 


Performance improvements      ARCH(15) - Vector instructions are now used to replace library calls with inline code and greatly improve the performance of the code generated for:   The HEXENCODE and HEXDECODE built-in functions. 
 The BASE64ENCODE and BASE64DECODE built-in functions. 
 Some BIT assignments 

 The compiler will generate inline code for many more instances of the REPATTERN built-in function, including cases where DDD elements are used and where MMM or MMM are used. 


Usability enhancements        The members IBMZLIBD, IBMZLIBP, and IBMZLIBS in the samples library illustrate how to use ZLIB compression code from PL/I. 
 The compiler now flags more code that might cause storage problems. In particular, it detects and flags code which uses a pointer that is assigned the address of one variable but is used as the base for a variable of greater size. 


Compiler option enhancements    
 Modified compiler options:   The new BASE64 suboption of the USAGE option lets you choose the last 2 characters in the base-64 "alphabet", either the standard + and / or the URL characters - and \_. 
 The new HEXDECODE suboption of the USAGE option lets you ask for much better performance (at the expense of validity checking) for the HEXDECODE built-in functions. 
 The new NOPUT suboption of the RULES option makes it easier to keep unwanted PUT statements out of production code. 
 The new DCLS suboption of the XINFO option generates a file containing declares of all external routines, and that makes it much easier to start using the existing RULES(NOLAXINTERFACE) option in order to catch nasty mismatching interface problems. 
 The existing CASE(ASIS) option has been extended to include data generated for the XINFO(SYN) and XINFO(SYM) options.
