Content: Storing the data     
 After collecting the data, the Tivoli Workload Scheduler for z/OS (OPC) component stores the data in data tables in the  IBM Z Performance and Capacity Analytics   database. As it updates the tables, the component uses the OPC_WORKSTATION lookup table to convert the Tivoli Workload Scheduler for z/OS workstation name to a workstation type.  Figure 105  shows which data tables contain values from the lookup table. 
 Figure 1. Tivoli Workload Scheduler for z/OS (OPC) lookup table data     The Tivoli Workload Scheduler for z/OS (OPC) component uses the DAY_OF_WEEK, PERIOD_PLAN, and SPECIAL_DAY control tables to update the data tables. For information on the control tables, refer to the  Administration Guide and Reference . 
 For detailed information about the data tables the component updates and the lookup table it uses, see  Data tables, views, and lookup tables .
