Content: Business event processing   Use this information to understand  business event processing  for the  z/TPF system . 

 What is business event processing?  A  business event  is anything that happens that is significant to a system.  Business event processing  is the capture, enrichment, formatting and emission of events, the subsequent routing and any further processing of emitted events (sometimes in combination with other events), and the consumption of the processed events. 

 How business event processing can help your business  You can use  business event processing  to enhance governance for standards compliance, and to monitor business processing.  Business event processing  enables detection of business situations, providing early and intelligent insight to assist you in making timely and effective business decisions. 

 z/TPF and business event processing  You can specify, capture, and transmit  business events  from the  z/TPF system . When a specified event occurs, the  z/TPF system  collects the data, and then formats and transmits the data to the event consumer through one or more dispatch adapters. 

 Plan for business event processing  There are several aspects to consider when you use  business event processing . 

 Configuring and enabling business event processing  Before you can use  business events , you must configure and enable  business event processing  on the  z/TPF system . 

 Increasing the size of the IBEVCNTL format-2 global record  You can increase the size of the  IBEVCNTL format-2 global record  to hold  unordered user-defined dispatch queues  that exceed the current limit. 

 Defining and deploying business events  Before the  z/TPF system  can generate and process  business events , you must define and deploy  event message business event  artifacts to the  z/TPF system .
Business event processing
Removing a loosely coupled processor  When you remove a processor that uses  business event processing  from a  loosely coupled  complex, you must move the  business event dispatch queue  on that processor to another active processor. 

 Business event deployment descriptors   Business event   deployment descriptors  are specialized XML files that contain the characteristics for each  business event . These XML files must be deployed on the  z/TPF system  before they can be used. 

 Event message   The event message format is used to describe  business events  that are created by the  z/TPF system . The event message format for a  business event  is defined by the  DFDL schema file  specified by the <esEventMessageFormat> element in the  business event specification . 

 Enrichment programs  An enrichment program is an optional user-written program. You can use an enrichment program to modify event controls specified in the  business event specification  and to gather additional information about the  business event  that you want to pass along to the event consumer. 

 Business event format  You can format the  business event  based on a standard format or a custom format. The format is specified in the  business event dispatch adapter specification . 

 Dispatch adapters  A  business event dispatch adapter  is a transport mechanism that sends the formatted  business event  from the  z/TPF system  to the event consumer. 

 Troubleshooting  Use this information to understand, isolate, and resolve problems that are specific to  business event processing .
#

